  "question": "Which investigation tested the widest range of air flow speeds, and how wide was that range?",
  "status": "has_data",
  "claim": "SPICE (PSI-107) tested the widest range of air flow speeds in the PSI tables, from 0.66 to 85.28 cm/s, a range 84.62 cm/s wide.",
  "summary_student": "Among the PSI experiments whose tables give an air speed for each test, SPICE covered by far the widest span: its slowest air flow was 0.66 cm/s and its fastest was 85.28 cm/s, a spread of 84.62 cm/s. The next widest were the smoke-detection experiments SAME-R (8.1 cm/s wide) and SAME (5.0 cm/s wide).",
  "summary_professional": "Of the investigations with a per-test flow velocity in the snapshot (n = 549 tests across PSI-107, PSI-101 and PSI-102), SPICE (PSI-107, column Air Rate (cm/s)) spans 0.66 to 85.28 cm/s, a width of 84.62 cm/s. SAME-R (PSI-101, Inlet velocity (cm/s)) spans 0.0 to 8.1 cm/s (width 8.1 cm/s) and SAME (PSI-102, Air Flow (cm/s)) spans 5.0 to 10.0 cm/s (width 5.0 cm/s). Saffire-I, Saffire-II and Saffire-III each report a single flow value per table and therefore have no range.",
